---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<DocsLayout 
  title="Git Workspaces & Automated Project Registration" 
  description="Automated GitHub repository cloning, authenticated PAT credential injection, Obsidian project spec provisioning, and branch workflows."
  category="Workspace & Notes"
  prevPage={{ title: "Custom Commands & Aliases", href: `${baseUrl}/docs/custom-commands` }}
  nextPage={{ title: "Obsidian & Syncthing Sync", href: `${baseUrl}/docs/obsidian-sync` }}
>
  <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-info">
    <strong>📂 Fully Automated Project Onboarding:</strong><br />
    Whenever you clone or create a repository via the chatbot, the Agent Station automatically registers the directory, injects your PAT token into the git remote, initializes an Obsidian Project Spec file, and creates a Telegram Topic sub-channel!
  </div>

  <h2>📥 Cloning Repositories (<code>/clone</code>)</h2>
  <p>
    You can clone any public or private GitHub, GitLab, or Bitbucket repository in three seamless ways:
  </p>

  <ol>
    <li><strong>Direct URL Paste:</strong> In your private chat with the bot, simply paste any GitHub link (e.g. <code>https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi</code>). The bot automatically detects the git URL and clones it!</li>
    <li><strong>Autocomplete Prompt:</strong> Tap <code>/clone</code> in Telegram ➔ The bot opens an interactive input placeholder asking for the URL.</li>
    <li><strong>One-Line Command:</strong> <code>/clone https://github.com/owner/repo [custom-folder-name]</code></li>
  </ol>

  <h2>✨ Creating New Remote Repositories (<code>/newrepo</code>)</h2>
  <p>
    Create a new remote GitHub repository, initialize local git files, and push the initial commit in one step:
  </p>

  <pre><code>/newrepo my-awesome-app "Autonomous full-stack web application built on OMV"</code></pre>

  <p>
    The bot creates the repo on your GitHub account, configures <code>.gitignore</code>, <code>README.md</code>, sets the default branch to <code>main</code>, and pushes to origin.
  </p>

  <h2>🌿 Git Branch & Diff Workflows</h2>
  <pre><code># Check uncommitted git changes:
/diff

# List all local and remote branches:
/branch

# Create and switch to a new feature branch:
/branch feat/user-auth

# Pull latest changes from remote:
/pull

# Push current branch to origin:
/push</code></pre>

  <h2>🛡️ Automated PAT Authentication</h2>
  <p>
    When cloning from GitHub, the bot embeds your configured <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> into the git push remote URL:
  </p>
  <pre><code>https://x-access-token:&lt;GITHUB_PAT&gt;@github.com/owner/repo.git</code></pre>
  <p>
    This allows autonomous agents running in <code>/task</code> or Claude Code CLI to commit and push PR branches without prompting for interactive credentials.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
